// PropertyTree's string value shares a union with its list value, so the C++ sizes its string type
// as the list: `ImmutableStringTemplate<sizeof(std::vector<PropertyTree>)>`. With MSVC's vector
// (24 bytes in release, 32 in debug) that is also big enough for what an ImmutableString holds:
// a shared string (16 bytes) and its flag byte. kpp's Vector is 16 bytes (a pointer and two int
// counts), too small for that, so the size says both things it needs: at least the list's, and
// room for the shared string and the flag (17). PropertyTree grows by the byte; nothing in the
// game depends on its size in a debug build (its `sizeof == 50` assert is for release builds).
class [[members]] PropertyTree
{
public:
  [[replaces]]
  using StringType = ImmutableStringTemplate<std::max(sizeof(std::Vector<PropertyTree>), sizeof(std::SharedPtr<const std::String>) + 1)>;
};
